This PR adds APIs for documenting validation rules. This allows you can describe how Scramble should document your custom validation rules, or those Laravel validation rules which aren't supported out of the box.

Rules documentation support is enabled by implementing `RuleTransformer` and/or `AllRulesSchemasTransformer` and registering them.

## Rule transformers
Rule transformers transform a validation rule to a JSON schema in the documentation.

Rule transformer is a class implementing `Dedoc\Scramble\Contracts\RuleTransformer` interface:
```php
use Dedoc\Scramble\Contracts\RuleTransformer;
use Dedoc\Scramble\Support\Generator\Types\Type;
use Dedoc\Scramble\Support\RuleTransforming\NormalizedRule;
use Dedoc\Scramble\Support\RuleTransforming\RuleTransformerContext;

class Ipv4Rule implements RuleTransformer
{
    public function shouldHandle(NormalizedRule $rule): bool
    {
        return $rule->is('ipv4');
    }

    public function toSchema(Type $previous, NormalizedRule $rule, RuleTransformerContext $context): Type
    {
        return $previous->format('ipv4');
    }
}
```

Now, this rule transformer can be registered:
```php
Scramble::configure()
    ->withRuleTransformers([
        \App\Documentation\RuleTransformers\Ipv4Rule::class,
    ]);
```

## All rules schemas transformers

Consider the `confirmed` validation rule. It requires a matching field named `*_confirmed` to be sent alongside the field being validated. This rule not only specifies a JSON schema, but also adds a parameter to the request.

To add support for such rules, implement the `Dedoc\Scramble\Contracts\AllRulesSchemasTransformer` interface and register a transformer like you would register a rule transformer. These transformers allow you to transform all resulting rule schemas.

```php
use Dedoc\Scramble\Contracts\AllRulesSchemasTransformer;
use Dedoc\Scramble\Support\RuleTransforming\NormalizedRule;
use Dedoc\Scramble\Support\RuleTransforming\RuleTransformerContext;
use Dedoc\Scramble\Support\RuleTransforming\SchemaBag;

class ConfirmedRule implements AllRulesSchemasTransformer
{
    public function shouldHandle(NormalizedRule $rule): bool
    {
        return $rule->is('confirmed');
    }

    public function transformAll(SchemaBag $schemaBag, NormalizedRule $rule, RuleTransformerContext $context): void
    {
        $schemaBag->set(
            "{$context->field}_confirmation",
            clone $schemaBag->getOrFail($context->field),
        );
    }
}
```

Thanks @chrisvanlier2005 for suggesting the API!
